I open my eyes, and I find myself at the same place as last night’s dream…
Somehow it feels warmer… softer…
…
\doctor: L3XA!!! Are you here?!
join alien (sonho/feliz e olho fechado) center
alien: Dr. Daphnis, you found me here again.
\doctor: Does that mean that this place is real, then?
alien (sonho/feliz e olho aberto): Yes. We are projecting our minds across space and time.
alien: We found each other, in this vast space
\doctor: Why am I just seeing you now? You were a voice before.
alien (sonho/feliz com cabeça inclinada): ... Our connection has gotten stronger… We know each other better now. Isn’t that nice?
alien: We can meet here whenever we want. And I did promise you that I would show you the sights.
update alien (sonho/feliz e olho aberto)
\doctor: Actually, I’ve been thinking… you spent all your energy answering my questions, and I didn’t give you the chance to ask me anything… feels a bit unfair , you know…
alien (sonho/triste e boca fecada): ...
\doctor: Unless, of course, you have nothing to ask… there’s no point in babbling to you about myself just to bore you…
alien (sonho/feliz e olho fechado): No, no, it’s not that… I’m just surprised, that’s all… it’s very thoughtful of you… I do want to know you better.
update alien (sonho/feliz e olho aberto)
The way they says this stirs something inside of me. Suddenly I remember that I’m completely naked.
alien: You don’t have to cover yourself, my friend. You don’t need to hide anything. All you are showing me is your own your true self.
I glance down at my body. It’s full of stretch marks, veins, surgery scars. And other types of scars.
alien: The mind, when conscious, will always project things onto the body.
alien: It will create whatever image will help us survive, out there, in the world. Sometimes we need to show ourselves as better, smarter, prettier, than we really are.
alien: But here, you can truly let go of that baggage, and exist only as your true form.
\doctor: It’s not very flattering, is it?
alien: I thought you were telling me not to get attached to superficial first impressions.
\doctor: ... Well… [pause]do you want to know me better then? I don't know if the answers will make me look any better to you.
alien (sonho/triste e boca fecada): ...
alien (sonho/feliz com cabeça inclinada): What is your favorite memory?
alien: Already with the hard questions? Let me see…
- MOTHER
	jump MOTHER
- ACADEMY
	jump ACADEMY
label MOTHER
update alien (sonho/feliz e olho aberto)
# mudar essa parte da terra para "planeta natal"
\doctor: I remember when my mother took me on a trip to see the Aurora Borealis… all the way back on my home planet…
\doctor: I was sixteen at the time. My head was full of ideas about my future, and about myself.
\doctor: We had a little pet parrot that we would take with us everywhere. He was there too.
\doctor: When we finally found the lights, even our parrot stopped making any sound. As if he too knew that that moment was special.
\doctor: Mom told me that no matter where I went, I must always remember that moment.
\doctor: That the joy of finding new things would always be with me.
alien: So, did you find many special things in your life?
\doctor: I did. Found one now.
L3xa seems happy to hear this.
alien: So you were close with your mother.
alien (sonho/triste e boca fecada): I never met my own mother. My kind strays very early from our progenitors.
\doctor: I wonder what that’s like. Humans are very close with their parents… sometimes. I hated my dad, and didn’t want to see him again… not after the things he said about me.
\doctor: He said he lost his son… and would rather see me dead.
alien: Those are strong words… What happened? What did you do to your father?
\doctor: Nothing… except becoming myself. I don’t think you would understand gender.
alien: Maybe it’s like parents. I don’t understand, but I can listen
\doctor: They gave me a label when I was born. I was supposed to play that role my whole life.
\doctor: But as I grew, I realized that the label felt wrong. I wanted to change it. But not everyone is okay with that.
alien: That seems like too much pressure to put on a youngling. My people just let them loose in the universe, and we must find our own way, become our own person.
\doctor: You know what’s worse? I see my dad every time I go out to work. I see it in their faces, even the ones who are under me.
\doctor: They think I’m a freak. Each day, there’s less and less of us, because the glorious future that the Empire envisions has no place for people like me.
alien: They seem to have a place for me, though…
\doctor: What did you say?
alien: ...[pause] it’s nothing. Just stay with me here, and let’s enjoy the view.
I feel that there is something that L3XA isn’t telling me. I wish they could trust me. All I want to do is stay here with them for a long time…
leave --All--
